      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- Choose a voice and speed with a short sample.\n- Keep audio files you can play or deliver.\n- Transcribe with your configured compatible ASR service."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Open **Plugins** in the DSH desktop app and install `dsh-voice`. If the CLI is available:\n\n```bash\ndsh plugin --profile desktop add dsh-voice\n```\n\nFor the web profile, replace `desktop` with `web`. Restart that DSH profile after installation. The package’s DSH requirement is `>=0.2.1-rc.3`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Start using it",
      "text": "1. Start a DSH session in the workspace where you want the audio saved; ask it to check the voice tools.\n2. Provide text, language, voice and speed, for example: “Make a Chinese MP3 from this text; give me a short sample first.”\n3. Listen to the sample, generate the complete audio, then play or deliver the returned file.\n4. For transcription, configure your own compatible ASR service, provide a local audio file, then review the transcript.\n\nExample request："
    },
    {
      "section": "Start using it",
      "text": "> Make a Chinese MP3 from this text. Start with a short voice sample."
